  [PASS] S3 WHY THE BAND-PASS ESCAPES FP3's LEMMA: its argument is linear in U, so the second variation of 2 alpha^2 q(|grad V|^2) is [2Q' + 4 g^2 Q''] h_k^2 k^2/2 per unit amplitude -- the constitutive block C_L times h_k^2, k^2-order, no W''(dX)^2 term; a multiplier gate W(C_g U'') B carries B W'' C_g^2 k^4/2 (FP3 C1's anti-pressure, k^4 order) -- absent here by construction
         measured: band-pass second variation == (2Q' + 4g^2Q'') h^2 k^2/2: True; multiplier gate's W'' coefficient == B C_g^2 k^4/2: True
         reading:  health of (b) is the kernel's own (C_T, C_L >= 0) times h^2 >= 0; the epoch factor L(<K>_h) is a leaf average (FP3 C1 lemma: no local second variation)
  [PASS] S4 THE KERNEL FAMILIES (class e) escape FP3's lemma: (e1) q_r has a closed form with q_r' = nu_P2(s + y_r) - 1, q_r(0) = 0, a FINITE zero-field tangent C_0 = sqrt(1 + 1/y_r) - 1, and C_L = C_L,P2(y + y_r) - y_r nu_P2' > 0; (e2/e3) the cut-off ON THE TANGENT has C_L = c C_L,P2 + y (nu - 1) c'/y_th -- a sum of non-negative terms with c' only (no c''), so C_T, C_L >= 0 for EVERY m and y_th, and a ZERO zero-field tangent (m > 1/2); CONTROL: the same cut-off multiplying the ENERGY puts c'' into C_L and turns it negative for sharp cut-offs
         measured: (e1) max |q_r' - (nu(s+y_r) - 1)| = 2.8e-13, q_r(0) = 0e+00, C_0 = (-sqrt(y_r) + sqrt(y_r + 1))/sqrt(y_r), C_L identity True; (e2) C_L identity True, c' = m x^(m-1)/(1+x^m)^2: True, zero-field tangent (m = 4) = 0, min C_L (tangent cut-off, m = 1-32, 3 y_th) = 5.90e-93; energy cut-off: first C_L < 0 at (m, y/y_th) = [(8, 1.086), (16, 1.023)]
         reading:  reshaping the PHANTOM LAW (the tangent) monotonically is healthy by FP2 C3's criterion whatever its switch shape; FP3's anti-pressure comes from gating the ENERGY on a density-type variable, which (e) never does
    FRW (zero field) per class -- the tangent C_eff at k with the band-pass factor h(k)^2 = (e^{-xi^2k^2/2} - e^{-L^2k^2/2})^2:
      ungated core             C_eff = oo            -> E = alpha_c + 2 > 2: Hadamard ill-posed (FP5 C3)
      (b) band-pass alone      C_eff = oo * h(k)^2    -> E = alpha_c + 2 at every k with h > 0: ill-posed (the band-pass does not cure FRW)
